1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:01,829
Welcome to ResGrid Academy.

2
00:00:01,980 --> 00:00:05,950
In this lesson, we will plan
coverage and keep dispatch aligned.

3
00:00:06,130 --> 00:00:10,790
A paper duty schedule and a dispatch
roster can drift apart, especially

4
00:00:10,790 --> 00:00:13,000
when members sign up or trade shifts.

5
00:00:13,170 --> 00:00:16,900
We will explain the features,
the setup decisions, and a

6
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:19,019
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:25,340
A career department sets up A, B, and C
shifts, and a volunteer department uses

8
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:27,720
shift sign-ups for weekend duty crews.

9
00:00:27,969 --> 00:00:32,329
Shifts show who is on duty and can
drive dispatch, so calls page the

10
00:00:32,329 --> 00:00:34,299
people who are actually working.

11
00:00:34,450 --> 00:00:38,419
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:38,419 --> 00:00:40,859
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:41,719 --> 00:00:45,279
Shifts, shift schedules,
sign-ups and trades.

14
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:49,279
Create your shifts, assign
groups and members, and decide

15
00:00:49,279 --> 00:00:51,219
whether dispatch follows shifts.

16
00:00:51,449 --> 00:00:53,839
Availability also depends on shifts.

17
00:00:54,230 --> 00:00:56,469
Check access in the target department.

18
00:00:57,250 --> 00:01:01,840
Calendar, the department calendar for
meetings, events, and training nights.

19
00:01:02,199 --> 00:01:04,579
Add recurring meetings
and training nights.

20
00:01:04,799 --> 00:01:07,479
Availability also depends on calendar.

21
00:01:07,659 --> 00:01:09,899
Check access in the target department.

22
00:01:10,680 --> 00:01:12,020
New calendar event.

23
00:01:12,199 --> 00:01:14,470
Add an event to the department calendar.

24
00:01:14,659 --> 00:01:17,919
Have your rotation or duty
schedule and decide whether

25
00:01:17,919 --> 00:01:19,579
dispatch should follow shifts.

26
00:01:19,989 --> 00:01:22,669
Availability also depends on calendar.

27
00:01:22,849 --> 00:01:25,100
Check access in the target department.

28
00:01:25,860 --> 00:01:29,030
Work shifts, repeating
work schedules for staff.

29
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:32,580
Have your rotation or duty
schedule and decide whether

30
00:01:32,580 --> 00:01:34,259
dispatch should follow shifts.

31
00:01:34,639 --> 00:01:37,039
Availability also depends on shifts.

32
00:01:37,430 --> 00:01:39,669
Check access in the target department.

33
00:01:40,470 --> 00:01:43,369
For the training scenario,
work in this order.

34
00:01:43,570 --> 00:01:48,339
Step one: Create an assigned or sign-up
shift with groups and staffing needs.

35
00:01:48,579 --> 00:01:53,150
Step two: Have demo members sign up
or complete a trade where supported.

36
00:01:53,369 --> 00:01:57,300
Step three: Review whether dispatch
follows groups or shifts and

37
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:59,339
confirm the calendar time zone.

38
00:02:00,129 --> 00:02:01,779
Now verify the result.

39
00:02:02,029 --> 00:02:05,119
Compare the scheduled roster
with the people dispatch would

40
00:02:05,119 --> 00:02:06,829
include at the selected time.

41
00:02:07,029 --> 00:02:10,019
Check trade completion and
the visible duty coverage.

42
00:02:10,199 --> 00:02:13,979
A common problem to watch
for: A calendar event is not

43
00:02:13,979 --> 00:02:15,909
automatically a duty assignment.

44
00:02:16,119 --> 00:02:19,879
Shift dispatch behavior must be
reviewed on dispatch settings.

45
00:02:20,679 --> 00:02:22,539
Your practice task is simple.

46
00:02:22,739 --> 00:02:24,549
Schedule a weekend duty crew.

47
00:02:24,729 --> 00:02:28,569
Change one assignment and
verify the expected roster.

48
00:02:28,759 --> 00:02:31,419
Track unfilled slots
and unresolved trades.

49
00:02:31,619 --> 00:02:36,140
Record the result, who owns the
follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

50
00:02:36,279 --> 00:02:40,229
Use the linked feature scripts for
the detailed screen recording plan.
